# Intro
Reproduces STARBENCH's (Bisbas et al. 2015, MNRAS 453, 1324, arXiv:1507.05621) late-phase D-type expansion test: a single ionizing source at the center of a uniform pure-hydrogen medium (`n_H ~ 3115 cm^-3`, `Q_H = 1e49` photons/s). Validated against STARBENCH's own semi-empirical solution (Eqns 8, 11, 28, 29: a blend of the pressure-driven and shell-inertia ODEs), not the classical Spitzer (1978) formula the sibling `../StromgrenSphere/` example uses (Spitzer over-predicts at late times, which is why STARBENCH exists). 

## Temperature
STARBENCH assumes a flat `T_i=1e4 K` / `T_o=1e3 K` two-temperature medium. This code computes `T_i` from metallicity instead; at `Z=0` (this example's default) it gives `T_i~47500 K`. To match STARBENCH's own convention, build with the flag below. `SPH:minimal_temperature=1000` floors the neutral gas at `T_o` regardless of build (already set in `params.yml`).

## Star mass
`star_mass=26.75 Msun` gives `Q_H=1e49 s^-1` in SWIFT-GEAR '''mass-luminosity fit.

## Resolution
`gas_mass=0.1 Msun` (default), ~770k particles.

## Star CFL condition
`Stars:CFL_condition_stars=0.5` in `params.yml` is looser than the code's
global `0.1` default: this example stress-tests HII ionization physics, not
stellar dynamical resolution, so it does not need a tight CFL bound on the
star's own timestep.

## Cadence
`HII_rebuild_time_Myr=0.01` (fixed cadence) is a numerical parameter, not
a physical one, but is not free to increase arbitrarily here: too coarse
a cadence updates the ionization state less often than the swept shell's
hydrodynamic response needs, and the front growth diverges from the
analytic solution. Keep at or below this value.

# Configure
Configuration matching STARBENCH's own `T_i=1e4 K` convention:
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_1 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle CFLAGS="-DIONIZATION_FEEDBACK_DEBUG_FIXED_IONIZED_TEMPERATURE_K=1e4"
make -j
```
`grackle_1` prices the ionizing photon budget against the neutral hydrogen
fraction from Grackle's own H/He species network rather than total hydrogen,
which the D-type expansion physics this example reproduces depends on. Dropping
the `CFLAGS` forcing flag builds with SWIFT-GEAR's own natural,
metallicity-dependent `T_i` instead, which does
not reproduce STARBENCH's `T_i=1e4 K` convention (see Temperature above).

# Run
```
./run.sh
```
Override any parameter via the matching env var, e.g. `gas_mass=0.05 ./run.sh` -- see `run.sh` for the full list.

# Checking
```
python3 starbench_analytic_check.py -s "snap/snapshot_*.hdf5"
```
T_i is measured from the run's own tagged gas, so the same command is
correct with or without the CFLAGS forcing flag above; pass
`--T-ionized-K` only to override the measurement (it warns on mismatch).
The front oscillates at this metallicity, so run-to-run and phase
differences of several percent at t=3 Myr are expected.
